 "name": "es-lr0",
 "purpose": "Stage-B low-rank ES (docs/rl-es-plan.md sections 5 and 10-11), run only if the cpi-x0 exploration probe finds no out-of-fold per-decision signal. From rl-m2 v39 with an es_basis: the top 3 principal components of each point's last hidden layer on the probe's own records (es_net.py --basis). Every option gets its bias plus 3 low-rank coordinates c<o>.<r> (its logit gains sum_r c[o][r] pc_r(h)), all in one joint block (4x es-m3's 168 coordinates). Sigma: calibrated on the probe records (mean |dP| 0.1 per coordinate, clipped [3, 15]) times sigma_scale 0.2 (es-m3 used 0.35 over a quarter of the coordinates; 0.2 keeps the total logit perturbation about 1.1x es-m3's). Same 160 games/iteration, pool, anchor gates and fitness as es-m3. Pre-set futility: after 6 updates (iterations 0-5), if the pooled gradient over all directions (es_propose.py) has split-half cosine <= 0.1 and |t| > 2 share <= 0.07, stop: no state-dependent signal at this budget.",
